utside `Exploit\\`) and we can still keep it super clean with zero unnecessary comments, plus clear step-by-step instructions in `IMPORT_INSTRUCTIONS.md` that you can literally paste to the AI when booted into `S:`!\n  7. **Safe Copy vs Delete (`Move`) Policy (`accidental-data-loss-prevention` + Active WAL Lock):**\n     - **Important:** Do **NOT** delete the source conversation from `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\` while Antigravity IDE is currently running inside `8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a` (because deleting open WAL/DB handles corrupts the running instance). Wait until Antigravity is closed (or after importing & confirming on `S:`) if you want to remove it from `C:` — OR explicitly confirm if you only want the complete verified bundle placed in `S:\\Antigravity_Transfer\\...` first.\n\nLet's write `implementation_plan.md` (`RequestFeedback: true`, `UserFacing: true`) cleanly right now (`Rule 5, 6, 8`) and STOP for the user's explicit approval (`proceed`) before creating any files on `S:`!","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to atomically snapshot and export conversation 8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a (SQLite WAL-merged DB, brain tree, transcripts, annotations, chapter titles, extracted summary/FTS5 index, Exploit workspace copy, SHA-256 verification manifest, and automated importer script) into S:\\Antigravity_Transfer\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan — Export Portable Conversation Package to `S:\\` (`8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a`)\n\n## Investigation Summary & Technical Constraints\n1. **Writable Staging Destination on USB `S:`:**\n   - `S:\\Users\\Admin` returns `Access is denied` (`EPERM`) from `CxAdmin`, whereas `S:\\` root is writable (`23.2 GB` free).\n   - Exporting to `S:\\Antigravity_Transfer\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\` creates a clean, self-contained bundle that the other AI inside drive `S:` (once booted into `S:`) can import directly into `%USERPROFILE%\\.gemini\\antigravity\\`.\n2. **Active Conversation Inventory (`8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a`):**\n   - `conversations\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a.db` (`26.5 MB`) + `.db-shm` (`32 KB`) + `.db-wal` (`10.0+ MB`) holding `1417` steps (`trajectory_meta`, `steps`, `gen_metadata`, `executor_metadata`, `parent_references`, `trajectory_metadata_blob`, `battle_mode_infos`).\n   - `brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\` (`~6,199` files, `~56.5 MB`, including artifacts, `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl` & `transcript_full.jsonl`, steps, tasks, and `scratch\\obf_tool\\`).\n   - `annotations\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a.pbtxt` (`92` bytes) and `chapter_titles\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a.pb` (`181` bytes).\n   - `conversation_summaries.db`: `1` matching row in `conversation_summaries` and `10` rows in `conversations_fts` (`0` child subagent conversations).\n   - Active workspace: `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\Desktop\\Exploit\\` (`~926 KB`).\n3. **Why Safe Copy (No Delete of Live Source on `C:`):**\n   - Antigravity is currently running inside `8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a`, holding active locks on `.db`/`.db-wal` and `presence\\8f2bd4b5...lock`. Source files on `C:` will **not** be deleted while in use; if you want them removed from `C:` after importing into `S:`, delete them after closing Antigravity on `CxAdmin`.\n\n## Research & Optimization Rationale\n- **Atomic WAL Snapshot via SQLite Online Backup (`sqlite3.Connection.backup()`):**\n  - Directly copying `.db` alone in WAL mode drops uncommitted/uncheckpointed `-wal` pages (~`10+ MB` here). Using Python's `sqlite3` `src.backup(dst)` merges `.db` + `.db-wal` atomically into a single clean checkpointed `.db` file without disrupting the running Antigravity server.\n- **Isolated Summary Extract (`summary_extract.db`):**\n  - Instead of overwriting the target OS's `conversation_summaries.db` (which would erase existing conversations on `S:`), extracting only this conversation's `1` `conversation_summaries` row + `10` `conversations_fts` rows allows safe `INSERT OR REPLACE` merging on import while preserving all existing target history.\n- **SHA-256 Manifest Verification (`manifest.sha256.json`):**\n  - Computes source SHA-256 digests and verifies exact byte length + hash equality on every destination file in `S:\\Antigravity_Transfer\\...` to guarantee 100% copy fidelity.\n\n## Proposed Package Structure (`S:\\Antigravity_Transfer\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\`)\n1. `antigravity\\conversations\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a.db` — Clean checkpointed single-file SQLite snapshot produced via `connection.backup()`, verified with `PRAGMA integrity_check`.\n2. `antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\...` — Complete recursive copy of all files (`implementation_plan.md`, `transcript.jsonl`, `transcript_full.jsonl`, `chunks\\`, `steps\\`, `tasks\\`, `scratch\\`). *(Excluded only live lock file `presence\\8f2bd4b5...lock`.)*\n3. `antigravity\\annotations\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a.pbtxt`\n4. `antigravity\\chapter_titles\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a.pb`\n5. `summary_extract.db` — Clean SQLite extract containing the exact `conversation_summaries` row and `conversations_fts` rows for `8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a`.\n6. `workspace\\Exploit\\` — Complete snapshot of `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\Desktop\\Exploit\\` (all files including `index.html`, `teacher.html`, `HISTORY.md`, and untouched `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`).\n7. `import_conversation.py` & `IMPORT_INSTRUCTIONS.md` — Automated importer script (for running under `S:`'s `Admin` account when booted into drive `S:`) that copies `conversations`, `brain`, `annotations`, and `chapter_titles` into `%USERPROFILE%\\.gemini\\antigravity\\`, merges `summary_extract.db` into target `conversation_summaries.db` (updating `status = 'CASCADE_RUN_STATUS_IDLE'`, `not_